<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $153.1 mln March 11.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $153.1 mln March 11.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $153.1 million surplus on March 11 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 11</p>
<p>Exports: $240.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $179.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $208.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $116 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $153.1 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.487 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.188 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.715 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.209 billion</p>
<p>    Net surplus: $805 million    ((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao</p>
<p>Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415)</p>
